<title>USA: 3Com stock down as Intel raises new threat.</title>
<headline>3Com stock down as Intel raises new threat.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of 3Com Corp and other computer networking companies weakened on Monday after Intel Corp unveiled inexpensive gear aimed at speeding links between personal computers arranged in workgroups.</p>
<p>&quot;This is aimed at 3Com most specifically,&quot; one analyst said, referring to Intel's plans. The chipmaker said it would introduce a competitively priced networking hub and a device with a single chip that could be used to reduce the cost of building networks while enabling workgroups to be upgraded to faster speeds.</p>
<p>3Com, down two at 21-1/4 in early afternoon trading, was the second most active stock on the Nasdaq.</p>
